# D-070: the repository checks out with the same bytes on every platform.
#
# On Windows, git turns text files into CRLF if `core.autocrlf=true` (the default on
# GitHub's Windows runners). Some tests compare files byte for byte — the `--json`
# snapshots, the interface contract, the accuracy sets — and a copy with CRLF would
# turn red while nothing in the code was broken. The result must depend on the
# repository, not on the machine's git settings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures and icons: no conversion, no line diffs shown.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.flac binary
*.ogg  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.m4a  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.m4s  binary
*.zip  binary
